.TH RMDIR 2 "August 1, 1992"
.UC 5
.SH NAME
rmdir \- remove a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
int rmdir(const char *\fIpath\fP);
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.IR rmdir 
function removes a directory whose name is given by the \fIpath\fP
argument.
The directory must not have any entries other
than \*(lq.\*(rq and \*(lq..\*(rq.
.PP
If the link count of the directory becomes zero and no process has
the directory open, then the space occupied is reclaimed by the system.
If any process has the directory open when the last link is removed, then
the \*(lq.\*(rq and \*(lq..\*(rq are removed and no new entries may be
created in the directory.
However, the space occupied by the directory itself is not reclaimed until
the directory has been closed.
.PP
Upon successful completion, the
.IR rmdir 
function marks for update the \fIst_ctime\fP and \fIst_mtime\fP fields of
the parent directory from which the named directory is removed.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
Upon successful completion, the
.IR rmdir 
function returns a value of zero.
Otherwise, a value of \-1 is returned and \fIerrno\fP is set to
indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
If any of the following conditions occurs, then
.IR rmdir 
returns \-1 and sets \fIerrno\fP to the corresponding value:
.TP 15
[EACCES]
Search permission is denied for a component of the path prefix.
.TP 15
[EACCES]
Write permission is denied on the directory containing the link
to be removed.
.TP 15
[EBUSY]
The directory to be removed is the mount point
for a mounted file system.
.TP 15
[EFAULT]
The \fIpath\fP argument points outside the process's allocated address space.
.TP 15
[EINVAL]
The pathname contains a character with the high-order bit set.
.TP 15
[EIO]
An I/O error occurred while deleting the directory entry
or deallocating the inode.
.TP 15
[ELOOP]
Too many symbolic links were encountered in translating the pathname.
.TP 15
[ENAMETOOLONG]
A component of
.I path
exceeds 255 characters,
or the entire pathname exceeds 1023 characters.
For POSIX applications these values are given
by the constants {NAME_MAX} and {PATH_MAX}, respectively.
.TP 15
[ENOTEMPTY]
The named directory contains files other than \*(lq.\*(rq and
\*(lq..\*(rq in it.
.TP 15
[ENOENT]
The named directory does not exist.
.TP 15
[ENOENT]
The \fIpath\fP argument points to an empty string.
.TP 15
[ENOTDIR]
A component of the path is not a directory.
.TP 15
[EPERM]
The directory containing the directory to be removed is marked sticky,
and neither the containing directory nor the directory to be removed
are owned by the effective user ID.
.TP 15
[EROFS]
The directory entry to be removed resides on a read-only file system.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
mkdir(2),
unlink(2)
